{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1119670-chronicles-of-fallen-london-crossover","id":1119670,"title":"Chronicles of Fallen London (crossover)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-23T16:38:06-07:00","id":1119670,"title":"Chronicles of Fallen London (crossover)","content":"So, got really enraptured with the Fallen London verse as of late. Played Sunless Seas, but then I got to the source material.<br /> <br /> For those unaware, Fallen London is a verse where Victorian era London was taken from the surface and dragged beneath the ground into a world untouched by the sun\u2026 and thus all sorts of strange stuff goes on because the rules of existence are suspended and effectively unenforced to the point that the rules of life and death are sometimes quite loose, and the the sale and trade of souls is something you can get a license for.<br /> <br /> Supernatural things often happen in the open here- infact, squid-like humanoids are a semi-rare sight in some places and you often meet animated clay men who act as labor. A common drug is<br /> <br /> <br /> It strikes me as a verse that might strongly go along with Changeling (being a place that has an open Goblin Market, and focusing on Stories), though there\u2019s enough room for loads of other things as well.<br /> <br /> My thought is that any campaign taking place in Fallen London (or any other Fallen City) would essentially have to play a bit like a Revealed game. There\u2019s not really much point to a masquerade if everyone knows weird shit happens, though that doesn\u2019t rule out secret societies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Vampires</span></b><br /> Vampires have one of the biggest changes. The sun NEVER shines here meaning that they effectively can go out wherever they want. They still would have to abide by certain rules and limits, but still, they don\u2019t have to worry about being in the sun, ever. And one weird quirk of the setting is that death\u2026 doesn\u2019t happen unless the body was completely destroyed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Werewolves</span></b><br /> Werewolves lose out kinda alot. A large part of their existence involves sky as a theme, and the natural order is really\u2026 weird in the Neath. Still, they would definitely try to adapt by treating the marshes as a woodland. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Mages</span></b><br /> As one of the quirks of the setting is that the natural order of the world is prohibited from being enforced because of where it is. In the cosmology of Fallen London, the stars are the beings that enforce reality and annilate things outside of how the world is supposed to be, but because of where Fallen London is, it is prohibited from it. I imagine mages in the Neath might have less issues with paradox or maybe none at all. Consequently, maybe there\u2019s less of them because they are in a place that lacks laws.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Prometheans</span></b><br /> The quest to define themselves as human gets strange here, especially since even normal humans are strange and because of Clay Men who act as laborers. Interestingly, they might have a tangled relationship to Unfinished Men, clay men who are lacking something but are incredibly dangerous because of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Changeling</span></b><br /> This is where the setting has the most crossover potential.<br /> <br /> To make a long story short, the big lynchpin than tethers this whole universe thing together is the Bazaar, which is sentient and trying to propose love to the Sun. Pretty much everything is able to be bought and sold at the bazaar, everything that can be. Love stories have serious Mark up there. Memories of a storm and bad dream too.<br /> <br /> Being in the Neath changes you, even if it's less drastic than what changelings go through. The royal family for instance has become somewhat inhuman and their dog ended up as something called the Eater of Chains.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m leaving out the other splats, because I have less idea on how to handle it; I also wonder how certain Fansplats act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:07:41-07:00","id":1119683,"title":"","content":"Well, life and death being jacked-up screams Sin-Eaters being interested in things.<br /> <br /> Mummies... how do the distorted laws affect them?<br /> <br /> How active is the God-Machine in Fallen London? Is this an accidental Hell, or merely another front in the rebellion?<br /> <br /> How does this interact with Beasts and the Primordial Dream?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:22:20-07:00","id":1119690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1119670-chronicles-of-fallen-london-crossover?p=1119683#post1119683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, life and death being jacked-up screams Sin-Eaters being interested in things.<br /> <br /> Mummies... how do the distorted laws affect them?<br /> <br /> How active is the God-Machine in Fallen London? Is this an accidental Hell, or merely another front in the rebellion?<br /> <br /> How does this interact with Beasts and the Primordial Dream?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well its all speculaton. And it's a crossover with an actual setting, so it's all up to anyone's best guess <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Still, in the Neath life and death are.... fluid in a way. Generally whsn people die they occassiinally wash up on the shores of the Stolen river alive. There are a fee ways to due permanently, generally it requires bodily evisceration. <br /> <br /> There's actually a subtype of person in fallen London called a tomb colonists, a man or woman so badly damaged yet still functionall that they essentially have to be bandaged up constantly to survive.... they live forever basically and only get slower as they age.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mummies in not sure how the weirdness interacts with them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and I just recalled. While I'm in sure of is active the God machine is in the Heath I know one place where it has no power at all. The Iron Republic, where everyone is free from all laws and tyrannies, that of man and nature.... And sense. Constitutional amendments rain down from heaven, you meet yourself constantly when you disembark, roads shift and turn at random and writing down what you see has a chance of causing an explosion when you read your report in another city as what you see is utterly impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to dreams I have no clue. You generally have a bunch of recurring dreams connected to.... some of the mysteries of the Neath","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 07-23-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T18:53:42-07:00","id":1119730,"title":"","content":"You really should look into Blades in the Dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T22:08:39-07:00","id":1119773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1119670-chronicles-of-fallen-london-crossover?p=1119730#post1119730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really should look into Blades in the Dark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm unsure about being able to afford that for a while. Saving up for something relatively big.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, so, on the Mummy front. One of the other things of the setting is that London is not the first City to Fall. It is actually the 5th. Whenever a new city falls, it slams down and crashes into the old one. <br /> <br /> The first one is kinda nameless/unidenfitied, but it is speculated it was the city Gilgamesh ruled. Maybe in a crossover, it's the Nameless City.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}